cockpit-wifimanager (1.2.0-1scorebird1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Modified by Nevco/Scorebird for NeST scoreboard devices. This is not an
    AllStarLink build. Changes relative to 1.2.0-1:
  * wifi-set.sh: select the NetworkManager-managed wifi device and quote the
    expansion, so it cannot word-split into an invalid nmcli argument list when a
    second wifi vif is present.
  * wifi-set.sh: create the connection profile in one call with the PSK included
    and autoconnect held off until activation succeeds, so NetworkManager cannot
    auto-activate a secret-less profile and fail it with reason 'no-secrets'.
  * wifi-scan.py: split scan output on the first colon only and skip blank lines,
    so a single SSID containing a colon cannot abort the entire scan.
  * wifi-set.sh, wifi-del-configured.sh, wifi-scan.py, wifi.js: stop, restore and
    account for nest-access-point.service, which shares the device's single radio
    with the wifi client. These parts are NeST-specific.
  * Declare Replaces: nest-cockpit (<< 3.6.0). The NeST firmware shipped this
    plugin's files inside its own nest-cockpit package until 3.6.0, so without this
    dpkg refuses to unpack on upgrade from such a version. Bounded so it expires by
    itself once 3.6.0 is released. No Breaks: that would make the co-installed
    nest-cockpit, which depends on this package, look unsatisfiable.
  * Corresponding source: https://github.com/garrettodom97/cockpit-wifimanager
    branch scorebird-nest-ap, tag scorebird-2.

 -- Byron Appelt <bappelt@nevco.com>  Wed, 29 Jul 2026 16:21:54 -0500

